Now, in a second example here, what we have done is we have added label to each and every resource here.

So the first server has a label where the key here is name and the value is CP Labs Gateway, and it also has a second label where the environment is production.

Now in a similar way, the second resource has a label where name is Cablelabs hyphen DB and the environment is production.

Similarly, if you look into the second environment here, the name is CP Hyphen DB and the environment is Dev.

Now from this label which is associated with a individual resource, you will be able to quickly find out that hey, the lower three resources which are created, they belong to the dev environment and now I can go ahead and stop all of these resources right away.

Now in order for you to know about this, having a label associated with this resource is very important.

